  "notes": "Cash basis. Governmental roll-forward uses fund balances (955,444 -> 994,995, p4) as beginning_cash/ending_cash. Transfers in 534,688 is the total column (net of eliminations); business-type transfers out (534,688) in business_type.transfers_net. Business-type: bond premium 1,043 (non-operating revenue) recorded in business_type.other_financing; roll-forward 3,101,573 + 1,976,017 - 1,368,835 - 534,688 + 1,043 = 3,175,110. Sales and other taxes 129,399 split by fund column: General 101,643 = p8 sales tax 94,858 + other state receipts 6,786 (1 rounding); Street 27,756 = p8 motor vehicle tax. Balance sheet uses the government-wide Total column on p1. Budget schedule p8 (all funds, budgetary basis) is recorded as detail; its transfers-in is an other financing item and the printed Total receipts includes it. Community development and Miscellaneous disbursement lines are zero and omitted. Read pages 1-8 of 8. Recheck: budget schedule 'Other local revenues' 2,273,210 split into governmental 304,697 (governmental receipts 1,075,676 on p4 less the p8 lines that tie to it, 770,979) and a business-type residual 1,968,513 (p6 proprietary receipts 1,976,017 differ by 7,504). Balance sheet (user 2026-10-27): governmental lines from the governmental funds statement of assets, liabilities and fund balances (p3), Total Governmental Funds column. Detail (user 2026-10-27): per-fund lines from the fund statements' columns (p4, p6) replace the combined schedule."
